[SIZE=6][B]CustomEnchants documentation[/B][/SIZE]
[B]Author: Lino[/B]

[SIZE=5][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]
Download the JAR from GitHub Releases, place it in plugins/ and restart the server. Supported target range: Minecraft 1.21.11 through 26.3, Spigot or Paper. Use Java 21 on 1.21.11 and Java 25 on 26.x. Folia is not supported.

[SIZE=5][B]Command format[/B][/SIZE]
Use /customenchants, /ce or /cenchants. Lowercase enchantment and equipment IDs are used in commands; rarity IDs use uppercase. Each subcommand requires customenchants.SUBCOMMAND. Player-facing commands are available by default; administrative commands default to operators.

[CODE]
/ce help
/ce enchants
/ce info <enchantment>
/ce shop
/ce tinkerer
/ce alchemist
/ce sets
/ce kits
/ce kit <id>
/ce rename <name>
/ce withdraw <amount>
/ce refresh
/ce inspect

/ce admin
/ce editor <enchantment>
/ce enchant <enchantment> <level>
/ce remove <enchantment>
/ce givebook <player> <enchantment> <level> [success] [destroy] [amount]
/ce random <player> <rarity> [amount]
/ce giveitem <player> <type> [amount] [value] [rarity]
/ce giveset <player> <id>
/ce giveweapon <player> <id>
/ce givekit <player> <id>
/ce resetkit <player> <id>
/ce setsouls <amount>
/ce open <player> <menu>
/ce reload
/ce effects
/ce diagnostics
[/CODE]

[SIZE=5][B]Additional permissions[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]customenchants.apply - apply tomes and merge enchanted equipment.
[*]customenchants.items - use special items.
[*]customenchants.kit.ID - claim a specific kit; grant this explicitly.
[*]customenchants.* - grant command and item permissions.
[*]customenchants.bypass.cooldown - bypass enchantment delays; operator default.
[*]customenchants.bypass.souls - bypass soul consumption; operator default.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Tomes and scrolls[/B][/SIZE]
Pick up a custom tome and left-click a compatible single equipment item in your inventory. A valid attempt consumes one tome. Success binds its enchantment; destruction on failure is disabled by default and can be enabled in config.yml (`general.break-on-failure`). An `aegis_scroll` protects once against a failed tome; an `eternal_scroll` retains the item after one death. An `unbinding_scroll` extracts one random extractable enchantment into a tome.

Anvil application costs three experience levels. Matching equipment items can merge their custom enchantments; equal tiers upgrade by one up to the maximum. Grindstones remove custom enchantments.

[SIZE=5][B]Shop, recycler and combiner[/B][/SIZE]
The enchanter shop sells random tomes by rarity. Rarity currency can be XP, LEVELS or MONEY. MONEY requires Vault and a compatible economy provider. Purchases are checked for inventory space before charging.

In the recycler (`/ce tinkerer`), select custom tomes or enchanted equipment from your inventory and click Confirm. One item is consumed from each selected slot, with configured XP rewards. In the combiner (`/ce alchemist`), select two separate identical-tier tomes of the same enchantment, or two `arcane_dust` items from the same rarity. Confirm to pay the configured XP cost and receive the upgraded result.

